                <pb facs="0900" n="780" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg780"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.48 Earthquake of 1931/1: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Panama</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Panama</hi></placeName> [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1931-03-31T14:05:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1931-03-31T12:00:00-05:00" when="1931-03-31"
                        >undated</date>].<lb/>[Received March 31, 1931—2:05
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>67. Tropical Radio reports Managua destroyed by earthquake this morning and now
                    burning. U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Rochester</hi> probably sail tonight
                    for Corinto. U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Sacramento</hi> standing by here.
                    Navy plane could be despatched tomorrow from Canal to investigate.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
